Meta tags are HTML elements in the <head> section that provide metadata about a webpage for browsers, search engines, and other services.

Meta Tag Provide essential information like page description, keywords, author, and character encoding.
Help search engines understand and rank web pages (SEO).
Control responsive behavior using viewport settings for different devices.
Used by browsers and web services to properly render and interpret content.




<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
​
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="description" content=
        "Free Computer Science Content" />
    <meta name="keywords" content="HTML" />
    <meta name="author" content="GFG" />
    <meta name="viewport" content=
        "width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
</head>
​
<body>
    <p>Meta Tags are used in this HTML Web page</p>
</body>
​
</html>
Syntax: 

<head>
   <meta attribute-name = "value"/>  
</head>
Attributes
Meta tag attributes describe what type of metadata is provided and how it should be used by browsers or search engines. The following attributes with their values are described below:

name: The name attribute is used for indicating the character encoding for the HTML Document.
http-equiv: This attribute is used to get the HTTP response message header (http-equiv Meta Tag Attribute).
content: The Content attribute is used to specify properties value.
charset: The attribute used to specify the character encoding of an HTML document is called charset.
Uses of Meta Tags in HTML
Meta tags in HTML provide information about a webpage, help search engines understand its content, control display on different devices, and improve accessibility and performance.

1. Specifying Important Keywords
The meta tag stores important keywords and information about a web page.
Search engines use this data to understand and rank the page in search results.
This process of improving page ranking is known as Search Engine Optimization (SEO).




<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
​
<head>
    <!-- meta tag starts -->
    <meta name="keywords" content=
        "Meta Tags HTML GFG Meta Data " />
    <!-- meta tag ends -->
​
</head>
​
<body>
    <p>This is a MetaTags Web page</p>
</body>
​
</html>
2. Automatic Refresh
A specified time will be mentioned in the meta tag after which the webpage will be automatically refreshed.





<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
​
<head>
​
    <!-- meta tag starts -->
    <meta name="revised about" 
        content="GeeksforGeeks" />
    <meta http-equiv="refresh" content="8" />
    <!-- meta tag ends -->
</head>
​
<body>
    <p>We are using refresh meta tag</p>
</body>
​
</html>
The web page will be reloaded after 8 seconds as mentioned in the meta tag.

